  "findings": [
    "Tab selection and folder toggle: no difference (vsync-quantized medians within 0.5 ms).",
    "Palette open is one frame slower in Rust/Metal (median ~31 vs ~17 ms); typing and closing are equal. Total Metal render time is ~3.6 ms per iteration and nextDrawable waits are negligible, so the extra frame is a vsync-aligned wait outside the Metal render path (window show/Core Animation), not yet localized.",
    "Browser-process CPU is ~24% higher in Rust/Metal (~30 vs ~24 ms per iteration); ~3.6 ms/iteration is in Metal scene rendering.",
    "Browser-process footprint is ~260 vs ~113 MB. Our Metal resources are small (8 surfaces, ~2-7 MB text tiles, ~9-19 MB drawables, ~18-29 MB device allocations). ~106 MB is \"Owned physical footprint (unmapped) (graphics)\" that appears on the first render pass; a standalone probe reproduces ~110 MB after one 64x64 render pass on this GPU/OS, independent of buffer count or target size, so it is a fixed per-process driver cost of in-process Metal rendering.",
    "Whole app process tree (browser+GPU+renderers): ~1300 vs ~1165 MB (+12%); the GPU process is similar (~508 vs ~523 MB).",
    "Mitigations to evaluate: render through the GPU process/compositor instead of an in-process MTLDevice, or a CPU/IOSurface path for small static surfaces; neither is implemented."
